    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) and **Seiya Suzuki** (75.03), our strongest plays by a significant margin. **Mickey Moniak** benefits from an elite +14% platoon edge against Mahle and favorable wind conditions that boost his score, while **Seiya Suzuki** leverages a superb 26-PA BvP history (+8%) and a prime matchup against Lodolo. **Brice Turang** (74.84) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) also surge into the mid-70s; **Brice Turang** is particularly vital for our speed-starved category goals, as his matchup against Chandler features a slow delivery window that creates a prime environment for stolen bases. **Vinnie Pasquantino** rounds out the elite tier, bolstered by a massive +16% park factor and a clean platoon advantage.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Josh Naylor** (52.95), who narrowly missed the cut behind the high-ceiling output of **Dalton Rushing** and **Edwin Arroyo**. While **Josh Naylor** provides a solid floor, the optimizer prioritized the positional flexibility and higher offensive potential of our starting options. We are also monitoring weather volatility closely, as **Edwin Arroyo**, **Austin Riley**, and **Seiya Suzuki** all face non-zero rain risks (32-39%). **Austin Riley** is further pressured by a wind-in factor that suppressed his projection, making him our most volatile start of the day. Finally, despite facing an elite arm in Yamamoto, we are rolling out **Corbin Carroll** and **Gabriel Moreno**, trusting their individual talent to overcome the SP hurdle, though we remain vigilant regarding the 3.38 xERA they are up against.",
